;; Seeds for the workspace corpus.
;;
;; A seed names a repo and the ADRs that are authoritative for it. It does NOT
;; contain the claims — the ingest derives every statement from a record it
;; reads at ingest time (manifest/west.yml, the ADR file itself, the GitHub
;; API) and refuses to emit anything it could not read.
;;
;; `:expect` is the innen discipline applied here: the seed says what the
;; resolved record must contain, and the ingest REJECTS a mismatch rather than
;; taking whatever came back. Without it, a renamed or moved repo would be
;; silently written up as if nothing had changed.
;;
;; What must never appear in this file: prose describing a repo. The moment a
;; human writes "kotobase is a fast graph database" here, that sentence has no
;; source and the whole record is worth less. Descriptions come from ADR titles,
;; which are themselves records.

{:seed-version 1
 :dataset "jiten-workspace"
 :lang "en"

 :entries
 [{:id :entry/kotobase
   :repo "kotobase"
   :title "kotobase"
   :topic-kind :artifact
   :expect "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase"
   :adrs ["2607265000" "2607032500"]
   :links [{:to :entry/kotobase-peer :kind :see-also}
           {:to :entry/kotobase-engine :kind :see-also}
           {:to :entry/kotobase-net :kind :see-also}]}

  {:id :entry/kotobase-peer
   :repo "kotobase-peer"
